On 12/15/05 6:34 AM, Jove wrote:
>   There is no better spell for a slow wizard to cast than Haste 
> Self.
> 
>   The beauty of the spell of Haste Self is that it can be cast
> "off-line", as it were.  Spell-friendly armor is not required 
> because the effect lasts, and can be pumped up.  (Find a closet,
> or just engrave a few dust Elbereths, strip off spell-unfriendly
> armor and cast the spell with maximum success rate.  Then cast it
> a few more times to pump it up.)  (I've had the spell of Haste 
> Self last more than 1000 turns after I've *forgotten* the spell.)
> 
>   With the spell of haste self I've happily worn mithril and 
> forgone casting spells during battle.  And it let's you examine
> all the boots you find (more boots found than any other type of
> armor except helmets, I think.) for the ones with the best 
> protection.  (Wearing +2 Dwarven boots in my current game.)
> 
>   Speed boots can be lost as well: lava, nymphs or scroll of 
> destroy armor (e.g. the original poster).  Even foocubi can 
> remove speed boots, leaving you dead slow until you get them back
> on.  Only (m)mf can remove a spell, and you've still got the 
> spellbook.
> 
>   And using a wish for +2 non-metal boots seems non-cost 
> effective since:
> 
>  a) Boots are the armor that least affect spell-casting.
>  b) Dwarven boots are plentiful and give 2 points of protection 
>     intrinsically. 
>  c) You're not guaranteed to get any positive enchantment from a 
>     wish.
> 
>   Granted, boots of speed require less thinking, but wizard
> is not the class for the hard of thinking.
> 
> 
>   A slow wizard with the spell of haste self is much better off
> wishing for SDSM than speed boots.  That way they're "very fast"
> and much better protected.  Especially if they look for the best
> footwear they can find.

Interesting. I've never seen an argument *against* speed boots before 
(of course, I realize this was in the context of "what to wish for"). I 
never knew that "haste self" had a cumulative effect (in terms of duration).

This suggests to me that the best combination on Astral is not speed 
boots, but rather haste self + jumping boots. Haste self gives speed for 
when melee is necessary, jumping boots allow you to travel even faster 
when you've opened up space (e.g., by wand of teleport).

